{"id": "EUVD-2026-25530", "enisaUuid": "fbbd1a9f-9514-35db-bcba-afeb75b0dedb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc: reject undecryptable rxkad response tickets\n\nrxkad_decrypt_ticket() decrypts the RXKAD response ticket and then\nparses the buffer as plaintext without checking whether\ncrypto_skcipher_decrypt() succeeded.\n\nA malformed RESPONSE can therefore use a non-block-aligned ticket\nlength, make the decrypt operation fail, and still drive the ticket\nparser with attacker-controlled bytes.\n\nCheck the decrypt result and abort the connection with RXKADBADTICKET\nwhen ticket decryption fails.", "datePublished": "2026-04-24T14:44:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:56:01", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/252157d939d179b5d767cb860ff8fa7f8723b67a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a75b3b361dd481d942c5f259a82d59718a41092c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b3a808cd0790b5075aaa2bc3588edf02cd71d352", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47073aab8a3a5a7b41c9bd37d2a3dcbeeccd6c8a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a149dcae23309df9de1c3b6b5d468610ef5ab7de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22f6258e7b31dba9bf88dce4e3ee7f0f20072e60", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58fcd1b156152613ba00a064a129fb69507ddd7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe4447cd95623b1cfacc15f280aab73a6d7340b2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-45qq-4p94-jp2v", "CVE-2026-31637"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.59, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01eb4938-8c24-3351-a9c3-068cb21653ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "17926a79320afa9b95df6b977b40cca6d8713cea <22f6258e7b31dba9bf88dce4e3ee7f0f20072e60"}, {"id": "029ad67e-7491-38b6-a694-e098c15c99ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.13"}, {"id": "07a9d89e-3c89-371b-b601-3ca7edc6d536", "product"